 Tell me, Metro, how did you manage to get control of our guard?

246
00:18:21,080 --> 00:18:26,730
 Right, back there, simple. I checked the walls, and when the guard came along, I created a sort of, um, a sort of interference.

247
00:18:26,730 --> 00:18:29,770
 I realized I could fuse all his circuits, so that's what I did.

248
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:34,500
 Then it was child's play to separate out the circuits we needed so he could operate.

249
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:39,420
 And then I went on to repair and reprogram these, and I must admit I'm not too displeased with the result.

250
00:18:40,140 --> 00:18:41,960
 Oh, you're really extraordinary, Metro.

251
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:46,170
 A ship. It's enormous.

252
00:19:09,130 --> 00:19:19,770
 Metro fighter craft.

253
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:23,660
 We have to make it to the asteroid belt. It's our only chance.

254
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:37,460
 Evasive action.

255
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:42,970
 There's danger.

256
00:19:48,260 --> 00:19:57,710
 The mission just reminded me. Remember Jurgle?

257
00:20:24,430 --> 00:20:27,690
 I wonder if that wasn't the risk that went...

258
00:20:27,690 --> 00:20:32,240
 ...of dust compared to Ceres with a diameter of 1,000 kilometers, or even Pallas.

259
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:37,080
 And you can count 13 or more of 300 kilometers diameter and 45,000.

260
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:39,660
 Stop it, please, Metro. This really isn't the moment.

261
00:20:39,940 --> 00:20:42,880
 All right. Trying to help. I'm going to bore you.

262
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:43,710
 Metro, look!

263
00:20:53,340 --> 00:21:00,760
 Another six. They know that we're here hiding, and they're out to get us.

264
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:05,100
 Only the asteroids prevent them from finding us, but they won't give up.

265
00:21:05,520 --> 00:21:09,800
 We know of their existence, and whatever their intentions, they can't let us go.

266
00:21:10,090 --> 00:21:12,030
 Okay, Metro, get ready to go into hyperspace.

267
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:16,150
 Into hyperspace in an asteroid belt, as they would say, conclusion illogical.

268
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:19,610
 I know it sounds crazy, but to stay here is certain death.

269
00:21:20,030 --> 00:21:22,890
 But we don't even have a protection screen on this mini monstrosity.

270
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:25,280
 Maybe, but that's not how I see it.

271
00:21:25,500 --> 00:21:26,300
 They won't follow us.

272
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:27,800
 They'd consider it illogical.

273
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:31,540
 We're going to try it, even if our chances are only 100 to 1.

274
00:21:31,900 --> 00:21:34,470
 Because staying here, we've no chance at all.

275
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:39,750
 To your seat.

276
00:21:39,830 --> 00:21:40,950
 We're going into hyperspace.

277
00:21:41,420 --> 00:21:43,200
 At least put on your space suit.

278
00:21:43,280 --> 00:21:43,900
 You never know.

279
00:21:43,980 --> 00:21:45,200
 It might give you some protection.

280
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,120
 Thank you, Metro.

281
00:21:47,240 --> 00:21:48,220
 That was nice of you.

282
00:21:53,040 --> 00:21:53,660
 Speed mode!

283
00:21:59,850 --> 00:22:13,950
 Sighted wreck of their ship.

284
00:22:14,050 --> 00:22:14,830
 No sign of life.

285
00:22:14,830 --> 00:22:16,290
 No other ships in sight.

286
00:22:16,290 --> 00:22:18,650
 No, Admiral. Sky is perfectly clear.

287
00:22:18,650 --> 00:22:20,400
 Very well. Return to base.

288
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:36,960
 Try to radio our position.

289
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:39,840
 Can't get into contact with Omega.

290
00:22:39,840 --> 00:22:42,750
 I'm not surprising with all the radiation the planet's sending out.

291
00:22:42,750 --> 00:22:46,880
 Well, I've had it. I can't stay awake. I think I'll sleep.

292
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:58,270
 You're here. I'm so glad.

293
00:22:58,270 --> 00:23:02,760
 Quickly, waiting for you to guide you.

294
00:23:02,760 --> 00:23:04,000
 Okay, Psyche, here I come.

295
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:08,540
 Motor's maximum velocity. Slow down now.

296
00:23:08,540 --> 00:23:26,080
 Here, Kim. I'm here.

297
00:23:26,080 --> 00:23:27,900
 You're where?

298
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:29,050
 It's wonderful.

299
00:23:29,050 --> 00:23:41,530
 Yeah, how are we gonna get down to them?

300
00:23:41,530 --> 00:23:43,550
 We can land on that large rock.

301
00:23:43,550 --> 00:23:45,740
 Seems flat?

302
00:23:45,740 --> 00:23:46,780
 There shouldn't be a problem.

303
00:23:46,780 --> 00:24:50,850
 Have you been hurt?

304
00:24:50,850 --> 00:24:52,480
 I don't know, Pyrrho.

305
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:53,600
 I guess I'm in shock.

306
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,600
 All I know is I hurt all over.

307
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:55,600
 Let's go.

308
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:57,850
 All right, Om, you take it easy, okay?

309
00:24:57,850 --> 00:24:59,240
 Dear poor Metro.

310
00:24:59,240 --> 00:25:00,430
 What can we do?

311
00:25:00,430 --> 00:25:02,360
 I'll come back and get him.

312
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:23,260
 I'm going back for Metro.

313
00:25:23,260 --> 00:25:37,280
 Life to him.

314
00:25:37,280 --> 00:25:38,310
 Very Psyche.

315
00:25:38,310 --> 00:25:39,310
 Maestro will fix him good as new.

316
00:25:39,310 --> 00:25:42,310
 I promise you he'll be going with us on lots of missions in the future.

317
00:25:42,310 --> 00:25:43,290
 You'll see.

318
00:25:43,290 --> 00:26:16,330
 It's your thoughtful wonders of Lucy.

319
00:26:16,330 --> 00:26:19,900
 Come take your place.

320
00:26:19,900 --> 00:26:21,370
 We're leaving soon.

